sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 + 5 (shared SSH identity), node.role_add and node.role_remove charts. swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-node-role-relocate-direct.yaml, docs/cli/node/role-relocate.mdx, docs/solutions/relocate-gateway-role.mdx.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 4, 6, 8, 9, 14, 15, 17, 18, 22 (no admit read-back, no per-stage asserts or projection step; target steps mirror role:add, source steps mirror role:remove).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:role:relocate
  %% kind: node.role_relocate
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane S icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Node 12<br/>gets the role
  participant S as Node 7<br/>gives up the role
  CLI->>GW: node:role:relocate 12<br/>websocket --from=7 --force
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:role:relocate 12 websocket --from=7 --force`
  %%> - syntax: `<node> <role> [--from=NODE] [--force] [--idempotency-key=KEY] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the target Node, by id or exact name, and the role: `gateway`, `websocket` or `metrics`
  %%> - `--from`: the source Node; omit it to use the current holder
  %%> - `--force` confirms the move; it is required without a terminal and with `--json`
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  opt role is swamp
    Note over GW: open: Nick decides<br/>live relocation of swamp
    %%> Today:
    %%> - refused with `validation.failed`: serve on the `swamp` Node runs every Swamp run, so a run cannot move it
    %%> Open:
    %%> - how a live move of the `swamp` role works; Nick decides
  end
  Note over GW: Validate, move the role<br/>role: provisioning · task #5180
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - the role is relocatable, and `--force` is given
  %%> - Node 7 holds the role; on a retry Node 12 holds it and `--from=7` names the same admitted move
  %%> - Node 12 and Node 7 are active, managed Linux Nodes; Node 12 holds no role that conflicts
  %%> - one role operation per Node: the Gateway holds the role lock for Node 12 and waits up to 2 minutes for a busy one
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - moves the `websocket` assignment to Node 12 with status provisioning; one assignment stays active the whole time
  %%> - copies role settings that Node 12 lacks, such as Reverb's `APP_KEY`; it never overwrites one
  %%> - for `gateway`: gives Node 12 an access grant to the `vpn` and `metrics` Nodes
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the role plan for Node 12, the removal plan for Node 7, the publication, certificate and Metrics changes
  %%> Secrets:
  %%> - role credentials go to the Swamp vault as execution copies; the inputs hold only their key names
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5180 recorded with the full intent; nothing has happened on a Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-role-relocate
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - both plans with their files and digests, and the vault key names
  %%> - the addresses and SSH host keys of Node 12, Node 7 and the fleet Nodes that publish; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - no step reads the intent back from the Gateway; the inputs are the intent
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5180
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Apply the role runtime<br/>cfgmgmt apt · file · systemd
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same steps as `node:role:add`: prerequisites, then the files, units and services of the role
  %%> - `websocket`: the Reverb service; `metrics`: Prometheus and Grafana; `gateway`: the Gateway Caddy site
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors over SSH from 209, in parallel where steps don't depend on each other
  %%> - each behavior's `check` replaces the per-stage read-backs
  %%> Rerun:
  %%> - a guard skips a part whose digest Node 12 already has
  opt role needs a certificate
    SW->>GW: Sign the role certificate<br/>operation:direct:certificate-sign
    %%> When:
    %%> - the role serves TLS with an Orbit certificate, such as `websocket`
    %%> How:
    %%> - a step creates the key on Node 12 and reads only the CSR; the Gateway signs it with the Orbit CA
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the one call a step may make to the Gateway
    GW-->>SW: Signed certificate<br/>leaf + chain
    %%> What happens next:
    %%> - Swamp writes the certificate beside its key on Node 12
  end
  SW->>N: Publish on Node 12<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt file · firewall
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - publishes the role's Caddy sites and PHP pools, validates them and reloads gracefully
  %%> - opens the role's managed firewall rules, such as `orbit:gateway-https`
  %%> - points the role's private DNS names, such as the Reverb host, at Node 12 through the shared DNS step on the `vpn` Node
  %%> - `gateway`: adds the private DNS route on Node 12
  %%> How:
  %%> - one `forEach` across the publishing Nodes
  %%> Order:
  %%> - Node 12 serves before anything leaves Node 7
  SW->>S: Withdraw from Node 7<br/>Caddy sites · firewall · grace
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - withdraws the role's Caddy sites, PHP pools and firewall rules from Node 7
  %%> - `websocket`: waits for old private DNS answers to expire, so clients reach Node 12 first
  %%> Order:
  %%> - runs only after Node 12 serves the role
  %%> Mirrors:
  %%> - the withdraw step of `node:role:remove`
  SW->>S: Remove the role runtime<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt systemd · file
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - disables the role's services and removes its units, managed files and certificates
  %%> - `gateway`: removes the private DNS route; Caddy and PHP-FPM keep running, so old clients still work
  %%> Keeps:
  %%> - role data, the Gateway checkout, its database, the Orbit CA and the SSH keys
  %%> How:
  %%> - official `@swamp/cfgmgmt` behaviors with `ensure: absent`, the same steps as `node:role:remove`
  opt a Metrics role exists
    Note over SW: Reconcile Metrics<br/>best effort · follow_up
    %%> When:
    %%> - a Metrics Node scrapes the role's exporters
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - validates and publishes the Prometheus config with the new target, then reloads Prometheus
    %%> If it fails:
    %%> - the move still succeeds; `follow_up` names `orbit node:role:add <metrics-node> metrics --converge`
  end
  SW->>N: Check both Nodes<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the role's services are active and answer on Node 12
  %%> - checks the role's units, files and sites are gone from Node 7
  %%> Why:
  %%> - one end check; the move only counts when both Nodes show it
  alt every step passes
    N-->>SW: role on 12, gone from 7
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed on both Nodes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; no step reports back
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>role: active · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `websocket` role on Node 12 becomes active, with the digest of each applied part
    %%> - Node 7 no longer holds it
    %%> - task #5180 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no match
    %%> When:
    %%> - a package, file, unit, certificate, publication, withdrawal or check step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark the role failed<br/>converge:STEP or remove:STEP
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the role stays assigned to Node 12, marked failed with the step's own error code
    %%> - task #5180 fails
    %%> On the Nodes:
    %%> - finished steps stay; there is no rollback
    %%> - a failure on Node 7 leaves the role serving from Node 12
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run `orbit node:role:relocate 12 websocket --from=7 --force` after fixing the cause; guards skip finished steps
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5180
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
